  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<strong><u><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/EM0026021_AnsExp_1_.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" style=\"width: 469px; height: 132px;\" /></u></strong><br /><br />The two electrons present in t<sub>2g</sub> orbitals can show d-d transitions between t<sub>2g</sub>&nbsp;and e<sub>g</sub> orbitals by absorbing visible light as CFSE is not very high due to weak NH<sub>3</sub> ligand&nbsp;field in an octahedral geometry<br /><br /><math> <mrow> <mtable> <mtr> <mtd> <msub> <mspace></mspace> <mrow> <mn>2</mn> <mn>1</mn> </mrow> </msub> <msup> <mtext>Sc</mtext> <mrow> <mn>3</mn> <mo>+</mo> </mrow> </msup> </mtd> <mtd> <mo>→</mo> </mtd> <mtd> <mn>3</mn> <msup> <mtext>d</mtext> <mo>∘</mo> </msup> </mtd> <mtd> </mtd> </mtr> <mtr> <mtd> <msub> <mspace></mspace> <mrow> <mn>2</mn> <mn>2</mn> </mrow> </msub> <msup> <mtext>Ti</mtext> <mrow> <mn>4</mn> <mo>+</mo> </mrow> </msup> </mtd> <mtd> <mo>→</mo> </mtd> <mtd> <mn>3</mn> <msup> <mtext>d</mtext> <mo>∘</mo> </msup> </mtd> <mtd> </mtd> </mtr> <mtr> <mtd> <msub> <mspace></mspace> <mrow> <mn>3</mn> <mn>0</mn> </mrow> </msub> <msup> <mtext>Zn</mtext> <mrow> <mn>2</mn> <mo>+</mo> </mrow> </msup> </mtd> <mtd> <mo>→</mo> </mtd> <mtd> <mn>3</mn> <msup> <mtext>d</mtext> <mrow> <mn>1</mn> <mn>0</mn> </mrow> </msup> </mtd> <mtd> </mtd> </mtr> </mtable> <mo>}</mo> </mrow> </math>&nbsp;<br /><br />Configurations and d-d transitions leading to colouration etc, are not feasible.",
